    "recommendations": "Reducing the concentration of heavy brush and shrubs near the structure and creating greater separation between surrounding vegetation and the building would improve defensible space and reduce fuel continuity across the property. Where brush is dense or in direct contact with the structure, clearing or thinning that vegetation could reduce exposure to the building and support firefighter access during suppression operations. Managing vegetation along the length of the driveway, including trimming overhanging growth and reducing brush concentrations at the margins, would help maintain clear access for emergency vehicles and improve evacuation conditions. The irrigated landscaping near the structure represents a valuable fuel break that should be maintained and preserved as part of an ongoing vegetation management strategy. Continuing to manage scattered trees and shrubs across the open terrain to reduce connected fuel pathways may further lower fuel continuity and support long-term wildfire resilience at this wildland interface property."
